after:
This is one example with two files. Save each labeled part in the named file, in the same folder, then compile main.cpp. Follow the guard when the header is included a second time.

```cpp
// File: score.hpp
#ifndef SCORE_HPP
#define SCORE_HPP
struct Score { int value; };
#endif

// File: main.cpp
#include <iostream>
#include "score.hpp"
#include "score.hpp"
int main() {
    Score score{3};
    std::cout << score.value << "\n";
}
```
